Feature: File Quality Check and Data Load to Unity Catalog

  As a Data Engineer,
  I want to validate the source sales file and load the validated records into the sales table,
  So that the data is accurate, complete, and can be reliably used for further reporting and analysis.

  Background:
    Given the source file is located at dbfs:/FileStore/tables/sales_20240611.csv
    And the target table is sales in Unity Catalog schema purgo_playground
    And the exception table is setup with schema to record erroneous data

  Scenario Outline: Validate and Load Data with Quality Checks
    Given a new sales file is available
    When the file is parsed for data quality checks
    Then it should identify and log the error records to the exception table
    And load the valid records into the sales table

    Examples: Data Validation Checks
      | Validation Check                   | Condition                                     |
      | Country Code                      | country_cd should not be null                 |
      | Quantity Sold                     | qty_sold should be numeric                    |
      | Product ID                        | product_id should not be duplicate            |
      | Date Format                       | Date should be in yyyy-mm-dd format           |

  Scenario: Validate Missing Values
    Given the sales file
    When a field "country_cd" is empty
    Then it should log the record to the exception table with message "country_cd should not be null"

  Scenario: Validate Numeric Fields
    Given the sales file
    When the field "qty_sold" is non-numeric
    Then it should log the record to the exception table with message "qty_sold should be numeric"

  Scenario: Validate Unique Product ID
    Given the sales file
    When "product_id" is duplicated
    Then it should log the duplicate records to the exception table with message "Duplicate product_id detected"

  Scenario: Validate Date Format
    Given the sales file
    When the date is not in "yyyy-mm-dd" format
    Then it should log the record to the exception table with message "Incorrect date format"

  Scenario Outline: Load Valid Data
    Given the sales file after quality checks
    When the exception records are removed
    Then it should load the remaining records to the sales table
    And use mergeSchema set to true

    Examples:
      | Field        | Data Type   | Validation Rule                     |
      | country_cd   | String      | Should not be null                  |
      | qty_sold     | Integer     | Must be numeric                     |
      | product_id   | String      | Must be unique                      |
      | sale_date    | Date        | Format yyyy-mm-dd                   |

  Scenario: Load Error Records to Exception Table
    Given validation process identifies error records
    When logging to exception table
    Then ensure mergeSchema is true for exception table
    And include error description message